<main id="main" class="help-page"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE HELP FOR THE JOURNEY</span><h1>How Cosine works</h1><p class="help-lead">Your driver's phone supplies the location. You don't need a dedicated tracking device.</p><div class="help-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>For students</h2><p>Open the dashboard, search for a registered bus and choose your pickup stop. The map shows recent shared positions. If the driver pauses, disconnects or stops reporting GPS, an old position is hidden after 45 seconds.</p><a href="/student" class="text-button">Open student dashboard</a></section><section class="panel"><h2>For drivers</h2><p>Get your assigned bus ID and private driver key from the fleet operator. Connect your bus, start the trip, then press Start sharing. Allow location permission when prompted. Set up before driving and keep the phone awake.</p><a href="/driver" class="text-button">Open driver tracking</a></section><section class="panel"><h2>Using phones across devices</h2><p>Both phones must open the same hosted HTTPS site. Localhost works only on the computer running the app. A phone cannot reach another phone through its own localhost address. Browser tracking can pause when the screen locks or the app is backgrounded.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Map and arrival estimates</h2><p>The map loads before any bus shares. Markers appear only for recent GPS positions. Pickup estimates use current speed and configured route geometry. Traffic and stop dwell times are not included; unreliable GPS withholds the estimate.</p></section><section id="privacy" class="panel"><h2>Privacy & demo access</h2><p>The sign-in and sign-up screens are previews. Any demo credentials work; passwords are never transmitted or stored. Demo identity stays in this browser tab and does not grant permission to publish locations. Public location sharing still requires a registered bus's private driver key.</p><p>Anyone with access to the student dashboard can view an actively shared bus position. Stop sharing before closing the driver page.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Nothing showing yet?</h2><p>The real fleet starts empty. Your operator must register actual buses and route/stop coordinates. Map tiles require internet access. If a tile service is unavailable, the app shows a map warning while bus details and trip controls continue working.</p></section></div></main><%- include('../partials/footer') %>
